            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0231" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/12–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dunn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-10T18:00:00+01:00">December 10,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:19 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4041. ReEmbtel 3991, December 7. Informed [that] Foreign Office has replied to
                    British memorandum that, while they agree with British reasoning, they consider
                    unity among Western democracies on issue of recognition more important. We have
                    been promised text of reply and shall forward it as soon as received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dunn</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
